# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-autocad-createobject-fails-on-runner — AutoCAD COM automation cannot start AutoCAD on the Windows runner (2026-09-27/28)
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: cad-runtime
#+DEPENDS: windows-access
#+BRANCH: -

* Observed

Every =alfe --autocad= (COM automation) run on PF5S26B in
=verify:epure-api:windows= on MR !336 (job 16774481586, 2026-09-28): the bridge
waits about 120 s and exits 4 with =ATTACHED=0 CREATED=0=, i.e. =GetObject=
found no AutoCAD and =CreateObject= failed. BricsCAD in the same job, on the
same machine, reached READY in 31 and 56 s. The AutoCAD run from a file on
MR !330 the day before failed the same way (130 s), while AutoCAD's symbol
probe earlier in that same job had worked. Another session recorded the
AutoCAD runner as unavailable on the same morning (commit 0b11a711).

pjb, 2026-09-28: =alfe -norc --$CAD --epure -x '(print (com_way "\\foo"))'=
works on Windows with BricsCAD and AutoCAD "when no other cad is running".

* What is known

- The ten acad.exe PIDs =Get-Process= lists on the runner (9164, 17640,
  21928, ...) are the known ZOMBIES of alfe-autocad-hung-instance-blocks-com-bootstrap:
  processes that exited days ago, kept in the table by a handle the COM
  service holds. They answer no COM call, so they are not what holds the
  registration -- unless one of them is in fact live.
- The COM error itself was not visible: alfe dropped it
  (alfe-autocad-bridge-com-error-dropped-on-ansi, fixed in alfe 2.2.146).
  About 120 s before failing is the signature of CO_E_SERVER_EXEC_FAILURE
  (0x80080005): COM started acad.exe and it never registered its class
  object -- typically a startup dialog on a desktop nobody sees, a licence
  prompt, or a crash at start. Not confirmed.

* Next

1. Re-run an AutoCAD job with alfe >= 2.2.146 and read the COM error it now
   prints.
2. If it is 0x80080005, look at the runner's desktop / AutoCAD's startup
   (licence, recovery dialog) -- that needs someone at the machine.

* Not reproduced — 2026-09-28, later the same day

=verify:epure-api:windows= on MR !341 (job 16776999021, alfe 2.2.146, the
version that prints the COM error): AutoCAD STARTED, in every run -- the
symbol probe, =-x= as typed and from a file all exited 0, and both verdict
runs printed T twice. There was no COM error to read. Whatever held AutoCAD
back in the morning (the ~120 s CreateObject failure) had cleared by the
afternoon, without a change on our side that could explain it: a transient
on the runner, most likely something on its desktop.

Suggested: close as not reproduced if it stays away; if it returns, 2.2.146
now prints the COM error, which is step 1 above. Left open for pjb to decide.
